Theorem RL-7: MaybeShared requires a sharing observation absent caller proof

  Preconditions:
    - DP-4 `needs_sharing_observation` is true exactly for MaybeShared.
    - DP-9 composes the DP-5 local result with IC-3 parameter uniqueness.
    - The projection may observe sharing by any validated mechanism.

  Soundness property:
    Forall owned MaybeShared value v at a mutation point:
      (P1) absent an IC-3 Unique guarantee, SharingObservationRequired.
      (P2) an IC-3 Unique guarantee plus DP-5 may admit same identity.
      (P3) the observed one-owner outcome may admit same identity; the
           multiple-owner outcome requires isolation.
    This theorem freezes outcomes and obligations, not IsShared, branching,
    copying, or representation.

  Proof obligation:
    Enumerate three cases:
      maybeshared_dynamic_check -> SharingObservationRequired
      maybeshared_param_unique_static -> SameIdentityAdmissible
      unique_no_dynamic_check -> SameIdentityAdmissible
    Coverage gate: 3 cases, each value-semantics checked.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl7_dynamic_cow)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: RL-7 checks the DP-4 observation gate and DP-9 outcomes without prescribing a runtime check or isolation mechanism
